  "title": "What Luxury Projects Really Demand From Metalwork — Through the Eyes of the Designer and the Owner",
  "excerpt": "Luxury boutiques, five-star hotels, premium residences and museums each punish a different metalwork failure. This in-depth guide sets out what designers actually specify (the signed sample, reflection integrity, 3 mm shadow reveals, ΔE ≤ 1.0 colour identity, node detailing, interface surveys), what owners actually live with (fingerprints, wobbling reflections, rattling seams, night-time glare, cleaning damage, premature ageing), and the specifications that satisfy both. It closes with a three-act conversation between a designer, an owner's development director and a factory project manager showing how a sentence becomes a number, a test and delivered evidence — plus the requirement-to-evidence matrix and six handover checks for each venue type.",
